Z||000000||ToddAsh||11-30-2001||12:05 AM|||| Just found a nice '86 GT metallic red with silver trim.Someone said this wasn't an original color on the '86.Can someone give me the met red codes or tell me what was available in '86.Picking up car Saturday morning need help quickly.Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||LS1swap||11-30-2001||07:51 AM||||Are you sure it is not an 87 for that was an 87 only paint scheme||||reg||1
Z||000002||ToddAsh||11-30-2001||08:35 AM|||| How do I check the year? The owner says its an original '86. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||ToddAsh||11-30-2001||08:35 AM|||| How do I check the year? The owner says its an original '86. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||11-30-2001||09:29 AM||||I'd ask for the VIN and run it through the decoder at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.net</A> <P>The paint code is printed on the Service Identification label in the front compartment.  The code looks like WA-XXXX where the XXXX's are the code.  Find that out and I'll be able to tell you what the original color is or should be.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ToddAsh||11-30-2001||05:08 PM|||| Does anyone have the codes for the '86 reds? I'm traveling a long distance in the morning and I have to eitheir take the car or pass.Just need the red codes and how to verify the year. Thanks. Todd||||reg||1
Z||000006||LS1swap||11-30-2001||05:55 PM||||I don't have them for an 86 but the 87 dark red metallic/Silver are WA9077 U77U 82D as far as telling the year look at the tenth digit of the VIN if it is a G it is an 86 and if it is a H it is an 87 correct me if I am wrong but don't the 86's have pontiac embossed in the rear bumper and the 87's do not||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||11-30-2001||07:33 PM||||WA-8553 Red (84-85)<BR>WA-8774 Red (86 & 88)<BR>WA-9077 Med red poly-metallic (87-88)<P>I believe these are all of the codes for red and that the year usage is correct.||||reg||3
Z||000008||mrfiero||11-30-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LS1swap:<BR><B>I don't have them for an 86 but the 87 dark red metallic/Silver are WA9077 U77U 82D as far as telling the year look at the tenth digit of the VIN if it is a G it is an 86 and if it is a H it is an 87 correct me if I am wrong but don't the 86's have pontiac embossed in the rear bumper and the 87's do not</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You are right about the G & H in the VIN (this is the easiest way to tell years apart), but not about the rear bumper.<P>The embossed "PONTIAC" on the rear fascia is only on the '84 Indy, '85 GT and '86-'87 SE......no fastbacks ('86-'88 GT's) have that feature (unless someone swapped out fascias).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||ToddAsh||12-01-2001||09:36 PM|||| Thanks everyone for your help.I bought the car today.It was a '86 GT that was repainted with the '87 color.A $4000.paintjob with All new rubber(doors,etc.) ALL new glass,Perfect Mint in & out,couldn't resist it.I have a '85 SE with 17,000 miles and it looks better than that.Was pinging on the highway on the way home but I'll start another topic for that.Thanks again,You guys are great.||||reg||1
